02:30:50.175 --> 02:30:53.830
is the first four if you
count the spin levels.

02:30:59.730 --> 02:31:03.320
Landau for filling
factor is bigger than--

02:31:03.320 --> 02:31:05.900
roughly bigger than 1/6.

02:31:05.900 --> 02:31:11.655
You have a fractional
quantum Hall liquids

02:31:11.655 --> 02:31:15.610
at the odd
denominator fractions.

02:31:15.610 --> 02:31:18.572
And the even
denominator fractions,

02:31:18.572 --> 02:31:25.370
you have is composite
fermion guess.

02:31:25.370 --> 02:31:34.450
If a composite fermion liquid
in the lowest Landau case.

02:31:34.450 --> 02:31:38.530
And you go to 1 for 5/2.

02:31:38.530 --> 02:31:42.140
Which you have very
likely, I think.

02:31:42.140 --> 02:31:45.360
Sort of it's p-wave paired.

02:31:50.764 --> 02:31:58.080
Then for n bigger than
2, the higher levels

02:31:58.080 --> 02:32:03.820
it appears I think the
current data sort of indicates

02:32:03.820 --> 02:32:07.910
Hartree-Fock ground
states has a lower

02:32:07.910 --> 02:32:11.910
energy than the fractional
quantum Hall states.

02:32:14.580 --> 02:32:19.080
I will not have
time to say anything

02:32:19.080 --> 02:32:22.290
about the winner crystal.

02:32:22.290 --> 02:32:26.610
But it's believed
in the clean system

02:32:26.610 --> 02:32:34.110
for the filling factor, less
than 1/6 there's no crystal.

02:32:34.110 --> 02:32:38.660
But in real life, of course,
the physical phenomena we see

02:32:38.660 --> 02:32:42.330
are always in play.

02:32:42.330 --> 02:32:45.480
The results of it interplay
between this order.

02:32:45.480 --> 02:32:47.820
And electron-electron
interaction.

02:32:47.820 --> 02:32:53.160
It turns out this crystal case
