02:38:22.440 --> 02:38:36.055
Now, I apologize for
this lengthy wordy thing.

02:38:39.130 --> 02:38:45.640
But I have a point to
make this afternoon that

02:38:45.640 --> 02:38:48.860
is summarized succinctly in it.

02:38:48.860 --> 02:38:56.620
So it is about my story of why
the fractional quantum Hall

02:38:56.620 --> 02:38:58.940
effect is important.

02:38:58.940 --> 02:39:01.990
It's fascinating
for lots of reasons,

02:39:01.990 --> 02:39:06.340
but it's important in
my view because it shows

02:39:06.340 --> 02:39:10.690
experimentally-- this is the
key word experimentally--

02:39:10.690 --> 02:39:18.040
that both particles carrying
a simple elementary fraction

02:39:18.040 --> 02:39:21.590
of the electric
charge of the electron

02:39:21.590 --> 02:39:27.230
and interacting by gauge
forces not postulated

02:39:27.230 --> 02:39:30.530
in the underlying
equations of motion

02:39:30.530 --> 02:39:35.650
can arise in an emergent
manner as collective effects

02:39:35.650 --> 02:39:39.640
from ordinary particles obeying
the ordinary laws of quantum

02:39:39.640 --> 02:39:42.840
mechanics.

02:39:42.840 --> 02:39:48.750
Now, both particles carrying
fractional quantum numbers

02:39:48.750 --> 02:39:52.290
and powerful gauge
fields between them

02:39:52.290 --> 02:39:56.140
are key postulates
of the standard model

02:39:56.140 --> 02:39:59.710
of elementary particles,
something that is allegedly

02:39:59.710 --> 02:40:04.360
fundamental in our universe.

02:40:04.360 --> 02:40:09.680
And as I'm going to
claim this afternoon

02:40:09.680 --> 02:40:11.810
the importance of
these experiments

02:40:11.810 --> 02:40:14.640
is that they impugn this idea.

02:40:14.640 --> 02:40:20.390
They suggest that maybe such
things in the universe itself

02:40:20.390 --> 02:40:23.240
could be emergent,
which is to say.

02:40:23.240 --> 02:40:26.390
Could not necessarily be
fundamental at all but just

02:40:26.390 --> 02:40:29.190
collective phenomenon.

02:40:29.190 --> 02:40:31.680
Frank Wilczek has a
wonderful name for this.

02:40:31.680 --> 02:40:35.540
He calls it solid
state imperialism.

02:40:35.540 --> 02:40:38.970
And I am the worst of the
solid state imperialists.

02:40:38.970 --> 02:40:42.050
At least, I hope so.

02:40:42.050 --> 02:40:46.980
Now, on that note,
let me start off

02:40:46.980 --> 02:40:57.050
with a thing that's been
a lot in the news lately,

02:40:57.050 --> 02:41:00.530
which is the theory
of everything.

02:41:00.530 --> 02:41:03.610
Now, this is not the
theory of everything,

02:41:03.610 --> 02:41:06.910
because there is
no light in here.

02:41:06.910 --> 02:41:09.880
And there is no nuclear
physics in here.

02:41:09.880 --> 02:41:12.340
And there is no gravity in here.

02:41:12.340 --> 02:41:15.560
And there are no weak
interactions in here

02:41:15.560 --> 02:41:16.740
and so forth.

02:41:16.740 --> 02:41:25.510
But for chemistry and the world
of physics at people scales,

02:41:25.510 --> 02:41:29.630
this might as well be
the theory of everything.

02:41:29.630 --> 02:41:33.730
And what I mean by everything
is shown down here.

02:41:33.730 --> 02:41:35.410
Now, look, everybody,
I apologize.

02:41:35.410 --> 02:41:40.720
I made this view graph
in Stockholm the day

02:41:40.720 --> 02:41:45.360
after we just had a press
conference that was completely

02:41:45.360 --> 02:41:50.580
monopolized by Professor Sin
who won the conops prize.

02:41:50.580 --> 02:41:53.430
And he had, of course,
done fundamental work

02:41:53.430 --> 02:41:55.110
in welfare policy.

02:41:55.110 --> 02:41:58.350
And you can imagine that
nothing sells better in Sweden

02:41:58.350 --> 02:42:01.300
than talks about welfare policy.

02:42:01.300 --> 02:42:02.730
And so I was kind of--

02:42:02.730 --> 02:42:05.160
I was feeling my oats
here when I finished out

02:42:05.160 --> 02:42:07.680
the things that the theory
of everything could describe.

02:42:11.860 --> 02:42:15.670
Notice what I meant
by Ebola virus.

02:42:15.670 --> 02:42:20.410
Now, one of the
things that these

02:42:20.410 --> 02:42:22.390
are-- by the way, those
of you who are not

02:42:22.390 --> 02:42:24.600
physicists, what is this?

02:42:24.600 --> 02:42:29.140
This is the elementary
Schrodinger equation

02:42:29.140 --> 02:42:31.570
for nonrelativistic matter.

02:42:31.570 --> 02:42:35.215
And H is the equation of
motion for this matter.

02:42:35.215 --> 02:42:39.010
It consists of kinetic energy,
of electrons, kinetic energy,

02:42:39.010 --> 02:42:42.910
of ions, coulombic
attraction between them,

02:42:42.910 --> 02:42:45.340
and also coulombic
repulsions between pairs

02:42:45.340 --> 02:42:47.200
of light particles.

02:42:47.200 --> 02:42:49.030
And that's it.

02:42:49.030 --> 02:42:55.730
Now, one of the things that this
theory of everything describes,

02:42:55.730 --> 02:42:59.560
it is alleged, is
this experiment.

02:42:59.560 --> 02:43:05.320
This is not von Klitzing's
original quantum Hall

02:43:05.320 --> 02:43:09.050
experiment, but it's
conceptually the same.

02:43:09.050 --> 02:43:11.860
So let's talk about
it as though it were.

02:43:11.860 --> 02:43:18.690
So let me remind everybody that
the way the experiments work is

02:43:18.690 --> 02:43:23.490
electric current is forced
along a sample that's typically

02:43:23.490 --> 02:43:28.490
about a millimeter, or even
several millimeters in size.

02:43:28.490 --> 02:43:32.000
In fact, this distance
here was one millimeter.

02:43:32.000 --> 02:43:34.080
In the presence of
a big magnetic field

02:43:34.080 --> 02:43:38.200
pointing out of
the board, then one

02:43:38.200 --> 02:43:42.490
measures two voltages
this one between this pad

02:43:42.490 --> 02:43:44.920
and the this one
between those two pads.

02:43:44.920 --> 02:43:47.050
That's the wiggly line here.

02:43:47.050 --> 02:43:50.236
And also between this pad
and that one, and that's

02:43:50.236 --> 02:43:51.235
the line with the steps.

02:43:53.866 --> 02:43:55.740
And those voltages are
measured as a function

02:43:55.740 --> 02:43:59.130
of field strength,
magnetic field strength.

02:43:59.130 --> 02:44:03.510
And what the effect is
that at certain values

02:44:03.510 --> 02:44:09.270
of the magnetic field are more
precisely certain ranges of it.

02:44:09.270 --> 02:44:12.810
The potential drop in the
direction of the current

02:44:12.810 --> 02:44:18.230
is going dies away to nothing.

02:44:18.230 --> 02:44:20.740
And at the same time,
the whole conductance

02:44:20.740 --> 02:44:24.470
which is across the current
path becomes constant

02:44:24.470 --> 02:44:29.140
and what Klaus discovered
was that the value

02:44:29.140 --> 02:44:32.020
of this constant, which
you can measure accurately

02:44:32.020 --> 02:44:39.470
because it's constant, is a
related to the current being

02:44:39.470 --> 02:44:44.790
forced by a hollow
resistance that's multiples

02:44:44.790 --> 02:44:45.900
of elementary constants.

02:44:45.900 --> 02:44:47.880
In this case, the
electric charge

02:44:47.880 --> 02:44:51.400
of the electron
and plugs constant.

02:44:51.400 --> 02:44:57.000
Now, as of this moment, the
accuracy of this experiment

02:44:57.000 --> 02:45:02.260
is about apart in 10 to
the 8, slightly less.

02:45:02.260 --> 02:45:13.300
And I ask you all to ponder
how accuracy that big

02:45:13.300 --> 02:45:17.340
could come out of
these equations.

02:45:17.340 --> 02:45:20.980
You see, everybody who's
solid studying quantum physics

02:45:20.980 --> 02:45:24.640
knows that computing things
like air, water, and fire

02:45:24.640 --> 02:45:29.230
from this underlying
equation of everything

02:45:29.230 --> 02:45:31.970
is a ludicrous undertaking.

02:45:31.970 --> 02:45:33.520
It's too hard.

02:45:33.520 --> 02:45:37.690
The equations here cannot
really be solved accurately when

02:45:37.690 --> 02:45:39.880
the number of atoms
exceeds about 10.

02:45:43.750 --> 02:45:47.680
Accurately means apart
in 10 to the 4, maybe.

02:45:47.680 --> 02:45:53.110
So beyond that, it
isn't possible to solve

02:45:53.110 --> 02:45:54.830
first principles a solution.

02:45:54.830 --> 02:45:58.920
So when we get
elementary constants,

02:45:58.920 --> 02:46:03.480
Planck's constant and e coming
out of a measurement with 10

02:46:03.480 --> 02:46:10.040
to the 20th particles in it,
we have to pause and ask, why.

02:46:10.040 --> 02:46:13.360
Why is it so accurate?

02:46:13.360 --> 02:46:17.530
Certainly, you can't deduce this
starting from the underlying

02:46:17.530 --> 02:46:18.340
equations.

02:46:18.340 --> 02:46:21.290
That's too hard.

02:46:21.290 --> 02:46:26.020
Now, you may or may not
know accuracy of this kind

02:46:26.020 --> 02:46:29.590
occurs all the time--

02:46:29.590 --> 02:46:31.420
all the time in physics.

02:46:31.420 --> 02:46:34.240
The first examples actually
come from chemistry.

02:46:34.240 --> 02:46:38.050
The ones I like to
cite, electrochemistry

02:46:38.050 --> 02:46:40.180
turns out to be a
very accurate way

02:46:40.180 --> 02:46:42.860
of measuring the electric
charge of the electron.

02:46:45.970 --> 02:46:49.210
However, the sexy
physics examples

02:46:49.210 --> 02:46:51.490
mainly come from
superconductivity

02:46:51.490 --> 02:46:53.420
and the Josephson effect.

02:46:53.420 --> 02:46:57.190
The Josephson quantum
of magnetic flux

02:46:57.190 --> 02:47:01.930
is the most accurate quantity
known in mensuration aside

02:47:01.930 --> 02:47:04.850
from the speed of light itself.

02:47:04.850 --> 02:47:08.620
And so there is plenty of
precedent in the physics

02:47:08.620 --> 02:47:12.970
literature for many, many
particles giving rise

02:47:12.970 --> 02:47:18.340
to accurate measurements
of elementary constants.

02:47:18.340 --> 02:47:24.430
And then all those cases we know
the reason for this accuracy is

02:47:24.430 --> 02:47:30.220
higher organizing principles the
matter itself is acting in some

02:47:30.220 --> 02:47:41.230
collective way that you cannot
deduce from these equations.

02:47:41.230 --> 02:47:43.730
You can't go deductively
from these equations

02:47:43.730 --> 02:47:47.420
to this behavior, because
the accuracy isn't there.

02:47:47.420 --> 02:47:50.150
So the intellectual
problem that's

02:47:50.150 --> 02:47:56.030
posed by questions like this
is, what is the principal?

02:47:56.030 --> 02:47:59.610
Why are these
experiments so accurate?

02:47:59.610 --> 02:48:01.670
Now, a part and 10
to the 8, you begin

02:48:01.670 --> 02:48:04.310
to think about
this a little bit.

02:48:04.310 --> 02:48:07.940
And you see that, well,
the theory of everything

02:48:07.940 --> 02:48:11.462
that I showed you
actually has corrections.

02:48:14.720 --> 02:48:20.480
The biggest one is here, as all
practical purposes, that spin

02:48:20.480 --> 02:48:24.170
orbit coupling and things of
that sort in this material

02:48:24.170 --> 02:48:28.400
would be parts in
10 the the 4 effect.

02:48:28.400 --> 02:48:31.310
The radiation field
actually is bigger,

02:48:31.310 --> 02:48:35.900
but it's subsumed by
normalization effects in QED.

02:48:35.900 --> 02:48:38.400
However, once we begin to
worry about these things,

02:48:38.400 --> 02:48:42.770
then we begin to worry about all
the other possible corrections

02:48:42.770 --> 02:48:45.460
to the experiment.

02:48:45.460 --> 02:48:48.010
How accurate can it get?

02:48:48.010 --> 02:48:50.930
What is limiting its
accuracy, if anything?

02:48:50.930 --> 02:49:02.360
Now, there is an
idea that is well

02:49:02.360 --> 02:49:05.220
known to people who worry
a lot about the quantum

02:49:05.220 --> 02:49:07.550
mechanics of empty space.

02:49:07.550 --> 02:49:13.290
And that is that empty
space isn't empty.

02:49:13.290 --> 02:49:17.220
Empty space is full of stuff.

02:49:17.220 --> 02:49:23.580
That is, the sum total of the
accelerator experiments that

02:49:23.580 --> 02:49:26.190
have been done since
the Second World War

02:49:26.190 --> 02:49:31.590
have told us that space is a
lot more like a piece of glass

02:49:31.590 --> 02:49:34.680
then it is ideal
Newtonian vacuum.

02:49:34.680 --> 02:49:36.220
It's filled with stuff.

02:49:36.220 --> 02:49:41.970
And so when I talk by
analogy between issues

02:49:41.970 --> 02:49:45.690
we have in the vacuum
of space, and issues

02:49:45.690 --> 02:49:46.860
that happen in solids--

02:49:46.860 --> 02:49:50.750
in fact, this analogy is apt.

02:49:50.750 --> 02:49:53.210
Empty space is not empty
in exactly the same way

02:49:53.210 --> 02:49:55.760
that a solid is not empty.

02:49:55.760 --> 02:50:00.530
So all these
corrections to the laws

02:50:00.530 --> 02:50:06.090
of physics in ordinary space
matter, at least in principle,

02:50:06.090 --> 02:50:06.656
they matter.

02:50:06.656 --> 02:50:08.280
And one of the
questions we have to ask

02:50:08.280 --> 02:50:12.720
is, why don't they
show up in mensuration?

02:50:12.720 --> 02:50:17.340
Why do all these-- why are
all these little corrections

02:50:17.340 --> 02:50:21.770
to the underlying
equations irrelevant?

02:50:21.770 --> 02:50:28.550
Now, the answer, of course, is
there's a principle involved.

02:50:28.550 --> 02:50:30.680
And in order to talk
about this principle,

02:50:30.680 --> 02:50:33.740
I have to remind you all
of something you know,

02:50:33.740 --> 02:50:35.660
or teach you it if you don't.

02:50:35.660 --> 02:50:38.570
And that is something
we call the principle

02:50:38.570 --> 02:50:39.920
of adiabatic continuity.

02:50:42.680 --> 02:50:44.340
So here's the problem.

02:50:44.340 --> 02:50:48.030
Suppose we've got something
we want to understand,

02:50:48.030 --> 02:50:52.790
and it's very complicated
like, for example, the Hall

02:50:52.790 --> 02:50:56.510
conductance, but we know
there's a principle involved

02:50:56.510 --> 02:50:58.640
that makes it exact.

02:50:58.640 --> 02:51:02.060
So we can imagine a
thought experiment

02:51:02.060 --> 02:51:06.540
where we perturb the
equations of motion slowly

02:51:06.540 --> 02:51:10.200
and interrelate
between lambda equals

02:51:10.200 --> 02:51:13.470
0, which is the
thing we're studying

02:51:13.470 --> 02:51:19.590
and lambda equals 1, which
is some idealized limit

02:51:19.590 --> 02:51:21.420
to the problem.

02:51:21.420 --> 02:51:24.450
Then, if it turns out
the thing we're measuring

02:51:24.450 --> 02:51:28.590
is constant, as I adiabatically
deform the equations of motion,

02:51:28.590 --> 02:51:32.130
then I can understand
what's going on over here

02:51:32.130 --> 02:51:34.500
by studying what's
going on over here.

02:51:34.500 --> 02:51:37.870
In solid state physics,
we do this all the time

02:51:37.870 --> 02:51:40.270
without calling it
this fancy name.

02:51:40.270 --> 02:51:42.100
We call it modeling.

02:51:42.100 --> 02:51:44.180
But I have to be a
little careful now,

02:51:44.180 --> 02:51:48.160
because the thing we're trying
to understand is an accuracy.

02:51:48.160 --> 02:51:50.170
And so we can't be
cavalier about modeling

02:51:50.170 --> 02:51:54.850
and have to really think
hard about what continuation

02:51:54.850 --> 02:51:57.760
principle allows us to
understand something

02:51:57.760 --> 02:52:01.150
exact in terms of a model.

02:52:01.150 --> 02:52:04.210
Now, the model that we--

02:52:04.210 --> 02:52:07.320
like, I would say, let's say
the model would be, I guess,

02:52:07.320 --> 02:52:09.240
this end of the line--

02:52:09.240 --> 02:52:14.050
that we like to think about
this problem in terms of

02:52:14.050 --> 02:52:16.160
is the one shown here.

02:52:16.160 --> 02:52:24.640
So what this is is ordinary
nonrelativistic electrons

02:52:24.640 --> 02:52:31.000
feeling a magnetic
field B and also

02:52:31.000 --> 02:52:36.230
moving in what we call a dirt
potential, or random potential.

02:52:36.230 --> 02:52:42.400
Now, at the risk of telling
a joke that will bomb,

02:52:42.400 --> 02:52:45.840
the dirt potential
is like pornography.

02:52:45.840 --> 02:52:49.990
I can't define it, but
I know it when I see it.

02:52:49.990 --> 02:52:52.070
In this case, the
random potential

02:52:52.070 --> 02:52:53.710
is something that
we could sketch

02:52:53.710 --> 02:52:57.260
but the truth is that, in
physics, we don't know how

02:52:57.260 --> 02:52:59.360
to define around a potential.

02:52:59.360 --> 02:53:04.910
We only know how to define the
behavior that you see in one.

02:53:04.910 --> 02:53:08.520
And the behavior that you see
in random potentials has a name.

02:53:08.520 --> 02:53:10.460
It's called localization.

02:53:10.460 --> 02:53:13.520
And localization is
an emergent principle

02:53:13.520 --> 02:53:18.560
that we know to be true, because
it's been seen in experiments

02:53:18.560 --> 02:53:19.550
many, many times.

02:53:22.080 --> 02:53:28.000
Now, before we get
to that, let's look

02:53:28.000 --> 02:53:29.980
at this random
potential that turns out

02:53:29.980 --> 02:53:35.380
is crucial to having
Hall plateaus.

02:53:35.380 --> 02:53:38.140
It's very easy to show
that if it's missing,

02:53:38.140 --> 02:53:41.240
then you don't have them.

02:53:41.240 --> 02:53:45.800
So suppose-- let's do that--
suppose the sample is system

02:53:45.800 --> 02:53:48.360
is translation invariant.

02:53:48.360 --> 02:53:50.300
So we have some
density of particles

02:53:50.300 --> 02:53:52.870
in there and a magnetic field.

02:53:52.870 --> 02:53:56.630
Well, then you all know
you can run past it,

02:53:56.630 --> 02:53:59.090
make a Lorentz
transformation, then

02:53:59.090 --> 02:54:00.770
by the relativity
principle, there

02:54:00.770 --> 02:54:03.110
will be in the moving
frame an electric field

02:54:03.110 --> 02:54:07.280
across the sample, a current
going along the sample.

02:54:07.280 --> 02:54:12.580
And the ratio of the
two after some algebra

02:54:12.580 --> 02:54:17.680
turns out to be the
number of particles

02:54:17.680 --> 02:54:19.510
per square centimeter
divided by the field

02:54:19.510 --> 02:54:22.970
strength times some
elementary constants.

02:54:22.970 --> 02:54:28.900
So measurements like this Hall
effect, measurements usually

02:54:28.900 --> 02:54:31.300
measure the particle density.

02:54:31.300 --> 02:54:35.200
And, in fact, this is a standard
and rather boring experiment

02:54:35.200 --> 02:54:38.350
that one does in
semiconductors to tell how

02:54:38.350 --> 02:54:41.810
many extra carriers you have.

02:54:41.810 --> 02:54:44.320
A corollary of
that idea, then, is

02:54:44.320 --> 02:54:48.770
that quantum Hall
effect can't occur

02:54:48.770 --> 02:54:51.310
in samples that are perfect.

02:54:51.310 --> 02:54:53.980
Because if the
sample were perfect,

02:54:53.980 --> 02:54:58.180
it would be measuring the
number of carriers in there.

02:54:58.180 --> 02:55:00.940
And the number of carriers in
the sample is not quantized.

02:55:03.520 --> 02:55:08.890
Now, let me now tell you
all about localization.

02:55:14.080 --> 02:55:18.110
This, unfortunately, is confused
by dimensionality issues.

02:55:18.110 --> 02:55:22.510
So let me tell you the old
lore back in the old days when

02:55:22.510 --> 02:55:27.360
people were thinking about
three-dimensional system

02:55:27.360 --> 02:55:28.060
semiconductors.

02:55:28.060 --> 02:55:33.170
In particular, the idea
of localization was born--

02:55:33.170 --> 02:55:35.770
it was born in the
mind of Phil Anderson.

02:55:35.770 --> 02:55:39.850
The basic idea of it is that
eigenstates of one electron

02:55:39.850 --> 02:55:42.670
quantum mechanics, which is
what we're talking about here,

02:55:42.670 --> 02:55:44.630
come in two varieties.

02:55:44.630 --> 02:55:48.250
They are extended states
and localized ones.

02:55:48.250 --> 02:55:52.680
Extended states are contiguous
from one side of the sample

02:55:52.680 --> 02:55:53.770
to the other.

02:55:53.770 --> 02:55:57.110
And they are capable of
carrying electric current.

02:55:57.110 --> 02:55:59.290
Localized states
are the opposite.

02:55:59.290 --> 02:56:02.280
They are not contiguous
from one side of the sample

02:56:02.280 --> 02:56:03.280
to the other.

02:56:03.280 --> 02:56:07.320
And they are not capable of
carrying electric current.

02:56:07.320 --> 02:56:17.480
Now, in an actual sample,
it is found experimentally

02:56:17.480 --> 02:56:20.510
that not only is
this true, but there

02:56:20.510 --> 02:56:26.660
is an energy scale called
the mobility edge below which

02:56:26.660 --> 02:56:28.700
all the states are
localized and above which

02:56:28.700 --> 02:56:30.590
all the states are extended.

02:56:30.590 --> 02:56:33.440
And the way the
system approaches

02:56:33.440 --> 02:56:37.850
these this edge is part and
parcel of the metal insulator

02:56:37.850 --> 02:56:43.170
transition in disordered
one electron problems.

02:56:43.170 --> 02:56:48.060
Now, there was, in the
old days lore about this,

02:56:48.060 --> 02:56:50.580
that you couldn't have
localized unextended states

02:56:50.580 --> 02:56:51.960
at the same energy.

02:56:51.960 --> 02:56:55.920
Because if you did, then the
tiniest amount of perturbation

02:56:55.920 --> 02:57:00.690
would mix then, and you'd
have two extended states.

02:57:00.690 --> 02:57:03.950
But nobody knew whether to
believe that law or not.

02:57:03.950 --> 02:57:06.090
So the way it came
down eventually

02:57:06.090 --> 02:57:10.780
was that this was
adopted as true,

02:57:10.780 --> 02:57:12.700
because the experiments
told us it was true.

02:57:15.360 --> 02:57:22.640
Localization is a phenomenon
that happens in nature that you

02:57:22.640 --> 02:57:27.020
cannot deduce from microscopics.

02:57:27.020 --> 02:57:30.710
You can get part of the way
there if you cheat and make

02:57:30.710 --> 02:57:34.220
some assumptions about
what a random potential is.

02:57:34.220 --> 02:57:36.690
But the truth is,
we don't do that.

02:57:36.690 --> 02:57:38.540
So the right way to
look at localization

02:57:38.540 --> 02:57:40.460
is not as a theoretical
ideas so much

02:57:40.460 --> 02:57:42.350
as an established
experimental fact.

02:57:44.960 --> 02:57:49.490
Now, what happens
in a magnetic field?

02:57:49.490 --> 02:57:52.540
Well, at the time of this
experiment, nobody knew.

02:57:52.540 --> 02:57:55.630
Nobody knew what had
happened, and there

02:57:55.630 --> 02:57:57.280
were some things we
didn't know, which

02:57:57.280 --> 02:58:04.350
was the random potential
should have taken Landau levels

02:58:04.350 --> 02:58:05.480
and broadened them.

02:58:05.480 --> 02:58:09.150
Landau levels are highly
degenerate manifolds of states.

02:58:09.150 --> 02:58:10.590
And the first thing
a perturbation

02:58:10.590 --> 02:58:14.560
does to degenerate states
is it breaks the degeneracy.

02:58:14.560 --> 02:58:19.880
So everybody
expected the density

02:58:19.880 --> 02:58:22.220
of states of this
one electron problem

02:58:22.220 --> 02:58:24.570
to look something like this.

02:58:24.570 --> 02:58:26.870
And, actually, I think
it's fair to say,

02:58:26.870 --> 02:58:30.050
in the beginning, everybody
expected everything

02:58:30.050 --> 02:58:32.990
to be localized.

02:58:32.990 --> 02:58:35.750
That it should have been
localized in the tail region

02:58:35.750 --> 02:58:40.940
was completely obvious from
anybody's point of view.

02:58:40.940 --> 02:58:45.190
That there should be
localization in the center

02:58:45.190 --> 02:58:47.960
was very non-obvious.

02:58:47.960 --> 02:58:53.840
The Klitzing experiments
told us that it was not so,

02:58:53.840 --> 02:58:58.080
that there were extended states
in the centers of these Landau

02:58:58.080 --> 02:58:58.580
bands.

02:58:58.580 --> 02:59:01.800
And the reason is because
it conducted electricity.

02:59:01.800 --> 02:59:05.097
So we knew that it must do so.

02:59:05.097 --> 02:59:06.680
There were extended
state bands there.

02:59:06.680 --> 02:59:10.040
But we didn't know much more
about that in those days.

02:59:13.100 --> 02:59:17.150
It was one year ago, I
guess, more like two years

02:59:17.150 --> 02:59:19.160
after the publication
of the famous gang

02:59:19.160 --> 02:59:25.190
of four paper
predicting or asserting

02:59:25.190 --> 02:59:30.110
that localization must be
complete in two dimensions.

02:59:30.110 --> 02:59:33.680
And we are, in fact, in two
dimensions in this problem.

02:59:33.680 --> 02:59:37.670
So many people felt
that localization

02:59:37.670 --> 02:59:39.860
should have been complete
and something else

02:59:39.860 --> 02:59:41.860
must have been going on.

02:59:41.860 --> 02:59:44.990
Now, as I said, the
experiments told us otherwise.

02:59:44.990 --> 02:59:46.880
And now, in the
light of hindsight,

02:59:46.880 --> 02:59:49.690
we understand that
localization physics

02:59:49.690 --> 02:59:54.610
is different in magnetic fields
than it is in their absence.

02:59:54.610 --> 02:59:57.370
In particular, this
problem has a density

02:59:57.370 --> 03:00:00.280
of states, which actually
looks like I've drawn it.

03:00:00.280 --> 03:00:04.150
It's tails of extent of
localized states separated

03:00:04.150 --> 03:00:06.760
by distinct bands
of extended ones.

03:00:09.300 --> 03:00:17.550
Now, how do you get perfection
out of imperfection?

03:00:17.550 --> 03:00:20.550
This is relevant to the
fractional quantum Hall effect.

03:00:20.550 --> 03:00:27.170
So let me lead you down
to this idea historically.

03:00:27.170 --> 03:00:34.070
Here is this now
infamous argument to me

03:00:34.070 --> 03:00:38.600
which accounts for
why localization

03:00:38.600 --> 03:00:41.610
makes exact quantization
of all conductance.

03:00:41.610 --> 03:00:44.540
And as Horst said,
the essence of it

03:00:44.540 --> 03:00:48.830
is that the system can be
made by a thought experiment

03:00:48.830 --> 03:00:51.080
into a charge meter.

03:00:51.080 --> 03:00:55.190
The thought experiment which
does that is illustrated here.

03:00:55.190 --> 03:00:58.810
So we imagine wrapping
the quantum Hall system

03:00:58.810 --> 03:01:00.382
into a loop.

03:01:00.382 --> 03:01:01.840
There's a magnetic
field coming out

03:01:01.840 --> 03:01:03.140
of the surface of this loop.

03:01:03.140 --> 03:01:04.348
I don't know how you do that.

03:01:04.348 --> 03:01:05.710
Just do it.

03:01:05.710 --> 03:01:13.160
And we will imagine filling
up these one electron

03:01:13.160 --> 03:01:15.230
states up to some
chemical potential

03:01:15.230 --> 03:01:20.390
that is in the local state band.

03:01:20.390 --> 03:01:27.490
Now, rather than computing
currents, which is hard,

03:01:27.490 --> 03:01:33.280
let us compute energies and then
take the adiabatic derivative

03:01:33.280 --> 03:01:35.560
of the total energy
of the system

03:01:35.560 --> 03:01:38.020
with respect to a little
bit of magnetic flux

03:01:38.020 --> 03:01:40.330
that's poked through the center.

03:01:40.330 --> 03:01:42.350
This is not hard to understand.

03:01:42.350 --> 03:01:44.307
It's just Faraday's
laws of induction.

03:01:48.440 --> 03:01:51.020
When you change the
flux to the center,

03:01:51.020 --> 03:01:55.710
there is some EMF that
winds around the loop.

03:01:55.710 --> 03:01:59.480
And if there is current going,
then it will do work on it.

03:01:59.480 --> 03:02:01.340
Why is this allowed?

03:02:01.340 --> 03:02:03.830
Well, it's allowed by the
fact that the system doesn't

03:02:03.830 --> 03:02:05.990
dissipate.

03:02:05.990 --> 03:02:10.190
So that if we are in a
region of localized stage,

03:02:10.190 --> 03:02:14.990
then the conductance, which
is to say the dissipative part

03:02:14.990 --> 03:02:18.630
of the response function,
has to be identically 0,

03:02:18.630 --> 03:02:23.020
because localized
things are insulators.

03:02:23.020 --> 03:02:27.430
And so that means that this
flux can be put into the loop

03:02:27.430 --> 03:02:30.010
and out adiabatically.

03:02:30.010 --> 03:02:31.690
So it's because
there's no dissipation

03:02:31.690 --> 03:02:34.630
that adiabatic
derivative makes sense.

03:02:34.630 --> 03:02:38.140
Now, while one is doing
this adiabatic derivative,

03:02:38.140 --> 03:02:42.150
the localized states do nothing.

03:02:42.150 --> 03:02:46.170
And the reason for that is
that since they go down,

03:02:46.170 --> 03:02:48.280
they don't go around the loop.

03:02:48.280 --> 03:02:52.680
They can't tell the difference
between addition of flux

03:02:52.680 --> 03:02:55.540
and a gauge transformation.

03:02:55.540 --> 03:02:58.360
So it's exactly true
that the localized states

03:02:58.360 --> 03:03:01.600
contribute nothing to
the adiabatic derivative.

03:03:01.600 --> 03:03:04.120
And for that reason,
I can just erase them,

03:03:04.120 --> 03:03:06.230
which I've done here.

03:03:06.230 --> 03:03:08.590
Now, we've got a
much nicer problem,

03:03:08.590 --> 03:03:11.740
which is little bands
of states separated

03:03:11.740 --> 03:03:17.050
by finite gaps in which the
chemical potential lies.

03:03:17.050 --> 03:03:19.750
Now, as I do this
adiabatic derivative,

03:03:19.750 --> 03:03:25.890
it is not possible for a state
to cross the gap adiabatically.

03:03:25.890 --> 03:03:28.120
The reason for that
is that if it did,

03:03:28.120 --> 03:03:30.880
it would be coincident in
energy with a localized state

03:03:30.880 --> 03:03:33.770
and, therefore, would
have to be localized.

03:03:33.770 --> 03:03:34.810
So that's out.

03:03:34.810 --> 03:03:37.480
So this little
localized state region

03:03:37.480 --> 03:03:38.800
here is like a brick wall.

03:03:38.800 --> 03:03:42.920
It prevents adiabatic
motion of states.

03:03:42.920 --> 03:03:46.510
And so that means
when I wind the flux,

03:03:46.510 --> 03:03:49.300
the only state
motion that's allowed

03:03:49.300 --> 03:03:52.400
is from one edge to the other.

03:03:52.400 --> 03:03:56.740
Now, the trick to making
this calculation simple

03:03:56.740 --> 03:04:01.120
is to make the sample big enough
that the adiabatic derivative

03:04:01.120 --> 03:04:04.780
can be replaced by
a differential where

03:04:04.780 --> 03:04:09.210
the denominator
is a flux quantum.

03:04:09.210 --> 03:04:13.570
Doing this means that
adiabatically changing slowly,

03:04:13.570 --> 03:04:18.390
slowly, slowly, stop, maps
the Hamiltonian back to itself

03:04:18.390 --> 03:04:20.340
up to a gauge transformation.

03:04:20.340 --> 03:04:22.800
And this means
that the system can

03:04:22.800 --> 03:04:26.310
have changed its energy
only by repopulating

03:04:26.310 --> 03:04:28.530
the original states.

03:04:28.530 --> 03:04:31.650
But that is only
possible at edges.

03:04:31.650 --> 03:04:33.810
Because only at
the edges are there

03:04:33.810 --> 03:04:35.820
states at the fermion energy.

03:04:35.820 --> 03:04:43.120
So the current carried is 1 over
C times the change in energy,

03:04:43.120 --> 03:04:44.920
which is the number
of electrons,

03:04:44.920 --> 03:04:47.200
the number of states, which
are transferred from one

03:04:47.200 --> 03:04:49.809
side of the sample
to the other times

03:04:49.809 --> 03:04:51.850
the chemical potential
difference between the two

03:04:51.850 --> 03:04:58.590
sides divided by a flux
quantum, which is the answer.

03:04:58.590 --> 03:05:03.870
So in this view of
accurate quantization,

03:05:03.870 --> 03:05:09.400
the proof, if you will, that
localization physics will not

03:05:09.400 --> 03:05:12.010
change the quantum
of Hall conductance,

03:05:12.010 --> 03:05:14.740
even though the
number of states,

03:05:14.740 --> 03:05:19.900
is changing, as is
their occupation,

03:05:19.900 --> 03:05:24.960
is that the experiment measures
the charge of the electron.

03:05:24.960 --> 03:05:27.600
The electron-- the quantum
of Hall conductance

03:05:27.600 --> 03:05:30.210
is quantized because the
electric charge of the electron

03:05:30.210 --> 03:05:31.810
is quantized.

03:05:31.810 --> 03:05:36.420
And the quanta can be viewed
in this context as the same.

03:05:36.420 --> 03:05:39.270
Now, that's historical
perspective.

03:05:39.270 --> 03:05:48.950
You can imagine my surprise,
great joy, actually,

03:05:48.950 --> 03:05:54.415
when I got this pre-print
from Horst and Dan

03:05:54.415 --> 03:05:56.790
announcing their discovery of
the fractional quantum Hall

03:05:56.790 --> 03:05:58.230
effect.

03:05:58.230 --> 03:06:00.630
So what you see here are--

03:06:00.630 --> 03:06:03.450
this experiment is just
the same as I showed you.

03:06:03.450 --> 03:06:07.680
We're sending a current along
the axis measuring voltages.

03:06:07.680 --> 03:06:09.900
The voltage drop in the
direction of current flow

03:06:09.900 --> 03:06:11.480
as, shown here.

03:06:11.480 --> 03:06:16.220
The Hall voltage between that
pad and that one is shown here.

03:06:16.220 --> 03:06:20.270
And down on the left, you
see Klitzing's effect.

03:06:20.270 --> 03:06:24.710
And then up here where there
should have been nothing,

03:06:24.710 --> 03:06:28.240
you see a new
feature developing,

03:06:28.240 --> 03:06:30.830
and a dip in the
parallel inductance

03:06:30.830 --> 03:06:34.640
corresponding to it
failing to get deeper

03:06:34.640 --> 03:06:36.010
as you lower the temperature.

03:06:36.010 --> 03:06:36.530
No, no.

03:06:36.530 --> 03:06:37.363
We checked all that.

03:06:37.363 --> 03:06:39.320
We checked for nonlinearities.

03:06:39.320 --> 03:06:41.480
It looks very good.

03:06:41.480 --> 03:06:44.390
You'll see it hasn't
gotten to 0 yet.

03:06:44.390 --> 03:06:46.371
In this experiment, it's
on its way, obviously,

03:06:46.371 --> 03:06:47.370
but hasn't gotten there.

03:06:50.370 --> 03:06:56.430
So I made a guess based on
my knowledge of these guys

03:06:56.430 --> 03:06:59.730
and also the way the
experiment was going, namely

03:06:59.730 --> 03:07:02.580
that localization physics
was also happening here

03:07:02.580 --> 03:07:04.530
and that it would
be complete when

03:07:04.530 --> 03:07:06.810
the temperature was lowered.

03:07:06.810 --> 03:07:10.990
Also, if you look at
this line with your eye,

03:07:10.990 --> 03:07:12.930
you'll center it
with your eye, you'll

03:07:12.930 --> 03:07:17.730
see it's already 1% accurate.

03:07:17.730 --> 03:07:19.891
And that was already too much.

03:07:19.891 --> 03:07:21.390
There should have
not-- there should

03:07:21.390 --> 03:07:24.420
have been no reason for
it to be 1% accurate, even

03:07:24.420 --> 03:07:25.990
that accurate.

03:07:25.990 --> 03:07:28.380
So there was every
reason to believe

03:07:28.380 --> 03:07:32.070
that the effect was the
same as Klitzing's effect,

03:07:32.070 --> 03:07:34.460
except at the wrong fraction.

03:07:34.460 --> 03:07:39.980
The filling factor, rather
than being integer, was 1/3.

03:07:39.980 --> 03:07:44.000
Now, Horst-- here is--

03:07:44.000 --> 03:07:46.440
the experiments got better.

03:07:46.440 --> 03:07:49.960
Here is a later one.

03:07:49.960 --> 03:07:56.190
So the guess was-- right here
is a later one showing the 1/3

03:07:56.190 --> 03:07:58.890
plateau, very well-developed.

03:07:58.890 --> 03:08:02.250
It's very, very
deep minimum here.

03:08:02.250 --> 03:08:08.160
And you can notice also
subsidiary fractions

03:08:08.160 --> 03:08:12.000
here at 2/5 and 3/7.

03:08:12.000 --> 03:08:18.940
Now, as the samples improved,
fractions of all sorts

03:08:18.940 --> 03:08:21.660
began popping out.

03:08:21.660 --> 03:08:24.930
And Horst likes
to say, well, what

03:08:24.930 --> 03:08:27.810
a neat thing it was
that good old Bob

03:08:27.810 --> 03:08:31.380
invented this equation
to explain it all.

03:08:31.380 --> 03:08:33.700
But the truth is, I didn't.

03:08:33.700 --> 03:08:36.880
And even worse than that, I
was really lucky-- in fact,

03:08:36.880 --> 03:08:38.290
the world was lucky--

03:08:38.290 --> 03:08:41.890
that samples were so lousy
when the original experiment

03:08:41.890 --> 03:08:42.640
was done.

03:08:42.640 --> 03:08:44.848
Because had we known about
all these other fractions,

03:08:44.848 --> 03:08:47.390
we would have been
very confused.

03:08:47.390 --> 03:08:50.680
So anyway, it was a
lucky break for everybody

03:08:50.680 --> 03:08:53.920
that this one just
happened to be

03:08:53.920 --> 03:08:59.000
the biggest one and,
therefore, the most obvious.

03:08:59.000 --> 03:09:04.770
Now, how accurate
is this experiment?

03:09:04.770 --> 03:09:06.590
Well, as I told you,
you can eyeball it.

03:09:06.590 --> 03:09:10.850
The original ones
were a percent.

03:09:10.850 --> 03:09:16.030
The modern error bar is
about a part in 10 to the 5.

03:09:16.030 --> 03:09:21.760
And most of us see
the only impediment

03:09:21.760 --> 03:09:26.890
to getting it better being
the temperatures to which you

03:09:26.890 --> 03:09:28.650
can cool the 2D electron gas.

03:09:31.360 --> 03:09:34.180
That means we have
the same problem

03:09:34.180 --> 03:09:38.050
with the accuracy of
this fractional plateau

03:09:38.050 --> 03:09:40.480
that we had with
the integer ones.

03:09:40.480 --> 03:09:44.350
That it's already too accurate
to be explained by modeling.

03:09:44.350 --> 03:09:47.410
There really must be
principal involved

03:09:47.410 --> 03:09:50.680
to make it so accurate.

03:09:50.680 --> 03:09:53.440
Unfortunately, the
localization principle

03:09:53.440 --> 03:09:58.990
that we knew won't work here
because any problem that

03:09:58.990 --> 03:10:03.340
can be adiabatic continued
to noninteractive electrons

03:10:03.340 --> 03:10:05.440
must have integer plateaus.

03:10:05.440 --> 03:10:07.630
That's the essence of
the thought experiment

03:10:07.630 --> 03:10:09.820
that I showed you.

03:10:09.820 --> 03:10:13.210
That means that this quantum
state, whatever it is,

03:10:13.210 --> 03:10:17.230
is not continual to
noninteracting electrons

03:10:17.230 --> 03:10:20.576
but is rather some sort of
many body effect that involves

03:10:20.576 --> 03:10:22.966
the coulomb interactions.

03:10:22.966 --> 03:10:33.450
Now, by far, the easiest
theory to make right now

03:10:33.450 --> 03:10:37.840
is that this effect is
the same as this one,

03:10:37.840 --> 03:10:42.010
except the thing
being localized is not

03:10:42.010 --> 03:10:44.760
an electron but a
piece of an electron,

03:10:44.760 --> 03:10:47.080
and elementary
excitation of the problem

03:10:47.080 --> 03:10:49.180
that has fractional charge.

03:10:49.180 --> 03:10:52.015
And please note that I'm talking
in the sense of the principle

03:10:52.015 --> 03:10:54.790
of adiabatic continuability.

03:10:54.790 --> 03:10:57.790
So I'm imagining a
limit of the problem

03:10:57.790 --> 03:11:02.470
where the objects, if you
will, elementary excitations,

03:11:02.470 --> 03:11:04.870
become noninteractive and free.

03:11:04.870 --> 03:11:07.150
In that case, we
have localization

03:11:07.150 --> 03:11:13.350
physics, just as before, but
not localization of electrons.

03:11:13.350 --> 03:11:16.350
But instead, localizations
of the elementary excitations

03:11:16.350 --> 03:11:18.960
in this state, whatever it is.

03:11:18.960 --> 03:11:22.890
Now, I can't emphasize too
strongly that the reason

03:11:22.890 --> 03:11:27.840
to believe this is
the experiments, not

03:11:27.840 --> 03:11:31.200
the theory that I'm
about to show you.

03:11:31.200 --> 03:11:33.630
The experiments
tell you that there

03:11:33.630 --> 03:11:36.240
must be fractionally charged
excitations in the problem

03:11:36.240 --> 03:11:39.780
because there is no other
way out of accounting

03:11:39.780 --> 03:11:42.160
for the accuracy.

03:11:42.160 --> 03:11:43.410
The accuracy is the key thing.

03:11:43.410 --> 03:11:45.210
There has to be principle.

03:11:45.210 --> 03:11:48.010
The principle you have
available is localization.

03:11:48.010 --> 03:11:51.630
Localization of things
deformable to electrons,

03:11:51.630 --> 03:11:54.960
free electrons, won't work
as a matter of principle.

03:11:54.960 --> 03:11:57.180
So, by far, the
easiest thing left

03:11:57.180 --> 03:12:00.270
is just to have a
new vacuum where

03:12:00.270 --> 03:12:02.850
the excitation is a fraction.

03:12:02.850 --> 03:12:10.530
Now, all that was left now
was to invent a prototype

03:12:10.530 --> 03:12:12.900
that everybody could understand.

03:12:12.900 --> 03:12:16.360
Now, you folks
probably many of you

03:12:16.360 --> 03:12:18.560
are too young to remember
that in those days,

03:12:18.560 --> 03:12:22.640
there was already a big
literature on fractionally

03:12:22.640 --> 03:12:25.370
charged excitations
that goes way, way back

03:12:25.370 --> 03:12:29.520
to papers on solitons
by Jackiw and Rebbi--

03:12:29.520 --> 03:12:31.160
done here, actually.

03:12:31.160 --> 03:12:33.290
And also, work done
by Bob Schrieffer

03:12:33.290 --> 03:12:38.370
at Santa Barbara
in systems which

03:12:38.370 --> 03:12:42.270
have-- will be called discrete
broken symmetries in them.

03:12:42.270 --> 03:12:45.690
So the idea that
there should be vacuo

03:12:45.690 --> 03:12:47.400
with fractionally
charged excitations

03:12:47.400 --> 03:12:48.900
is not originally to me.

03:12:48.900 --> 03:12:52.500
It's due to people who went
before me, chiefly particle

03:12:52.500 --> 03:12:54.360
physics and Bob Schrieffer.

03:12:57.060 --> 03:13:01.890
So one already knew that
the idea was not nuts.

03:13:01.890 --> 03:13:08.740
The only thing left was to
figure out what it might be.

03:13:08.740 --> 03:13:11.620
Now, I should tell you when--

03:13:14.460 --> 03:13:19.020
I knew about the
soliton work, and so I

03:13:19.020 --> 03:13:23.090
made a theory of
this effect based

03:13:23.090 --> 03:13:27.710
on an analogy with fractional
quantization in solitons.

03:13:27.710 --> 03:13:30.080
And I sent it into
Phys Rev Letters.

03:13:30.080 --> 03:13:34.340
And I like to say, thank
god the referee rejected it.

03:13:34.340 --> 03:13:38.180
I know later that this
referee was Steve Kivelson.

03:13:38.180 --> 03:13:43.024
And Steve pointed out, well,
that your discrete symmetry

03:13:43.024 --> 03:13:44.690
breaking that you've
made in your theory

03:13:44.690 --> 03:13:46.520
is really continuous
image rating.

03:13:46.520 --> 03:13:51.680
It's like the stripe idea,
and that means it's got a pin.

03:13:51.680 --> 03:13:56.360
And, therefore, it wouldn't
conduct electricity,

03:13:56.360 --> 03:13:59.640
and so the whole
idea is nonsense.

03:13:59.640 --> 03:14:01.050
So I got this referee report.

03:14:01.050 --> 03:14:02.883
And I said, well,
unfortunately, he's right.

03:14:02.883 --> 03:14:05.410
So I need to go
think about it more.

03:14:05.410 --> 03:14:08.340
So I thought, well, this thing--

03:14:08.340 --> 03:14:11.710
experiments are telling us it
has a great big energy gap.

03:14:11.710 --> 03:14:14.270
So when things have energy
gaps, you can get to first base

03:14:14.270 --> 03:14:17.860
in modeling them
just by brute force.

03:14:17.860 --> 03:14:22.560
So I thought, OK, let's try to
solve the problem by computer,

03:14:22.560 --> 03:14:24.220
starting with one electron.

03:14:24.220 --> 03:14:25.560
That I can do.

03:14:25.560 --> 03:14:28.380
Then let's do two.

03:14:28.380 --> 03:14:28.920
I did two.

03:14:28.920 --> 03:14:31.045
That turns out to be easier
than doing it on paper.

03:14:31.045 --> 03:14:31.780
[BELL RINGING]

03:14:31.780 --> 03:14:33.620
What does that mean?

03:14:33.620 --> 03:14:34.810
Nothing.

03:14:34.810 --> 03:14:36.980
Hello?

03:14:36.980 --> 03:14:39.840
Then 3, then 4.

03:14:39.840 --> 03:14:43.970
So the model Hamiltonian
one couldn't study

03:14:43.970 --> 03:14:47.780
is just a few electrons
that are repelling

03:14:47.780 --> 03:14:49.400
each other coulombically.

03:14:49.400 --> 03:14:52.310
And for balance, let's put
a little pressure in here

03:14:52.310 --> 03:14:58.130
to keep them in these
old calculations.

03:14:58.130 --> 03:15:00.900
There are two energy scales.

03:15:00.900 --> 03:15:04.610
There's a so-called cyclotron
frequency and coulomb energy,

03:15:04.610 --> 03:15:08.780
which is e squared over
the length associated

03:15:08.780 --> 03:15:12.620
with that harmonic
oscillator energy.

03:15:12.620 --> 03:15:16.760
And the limit we usually prefer
as theorists is this one, where

03:15:16.760 --> 03:15:20.330
the cyclotron energy is much
larger than the coulomb energy,

03:15:20.330 --> 03:15:22.790
even though in real
samples, we're not always

03:15:22.790 --> 03:15:24.840
deeply in that limit.

03:15:24.840 --> 03:15:27.620
But it doesn't matter because
of the adiabatic continuability.

03:15:27.620 --> 03:15:29.980
This is the right
limit to be in.

03:15:29.980 --> 03:15:34.910
So I studied, looked
at these guys,

03:15:34.910 --> 03:15:39.800
and solved them, and got
the wave functions out,

03:15:39.800 --> 03:15:40.990
and showed them here.

03:15:40.990 --> 03:15:42.860
There they are.

03:15:42.860 --> 03:15:46.529
These wave functions I'm showing
you are completely meaningless.

03:15:46.529 --> 03:15:47.570
I just like to show them.

03:15:51.530 --> 03:15:57.230
Then I found those, sure enough.

03:15:57.230 --> 03:16:01.820
The little cluster is kind of
doing what the experiments do.

03:16:01.820 --> 03:16:04.860
As you increase the
pressure going this way,

03:16:04.860 --> 03:16:08.680
the mean square error
changes and jumps,

03:16:08.680 --> 03:16:14.030
and the angular momentum
also changes and jumps

03:16:14.030 --> 03:16:15.800
as though it's contracting.

03:16:15.800 --> 03:16:20.990
It has preferred densities, and
it's contracting discretely.

03:16:20.990 --> 03:16:24.420
So I thought, that's good.

03:16:24.420 --> 03:16:30.590
Then I said, OK, well that's
what's happening then.

03:16:30.590 --> 03:16:38.010
Maybe something like this thing
down here is the ground state.

03:16:38.010 --> 03:16:41.990
So I knew this
function is exact.

03:16:41.990 --> 03:16:44.390
When the number
of particles is 2,

03:16:44.390 --> 03:16:46.340
it's pretty close when
the number of particles

03:16:46.340 --> 03:16:48.710
was 3, 4, or 5 and 6.

03:16:48.710 --> 03:16:52.040
So I spent several
weeks trying to prove

03:16:52.040 --> 03:16:53.480
that it was the
exact ground state

03:16:53.480 --> 03:16:56.480
of the relevant Hamiltonian.

03:16:56.480 --> 03:16:57.980
Relevant Hamiltonian,
in this case,

03:16:57.980 --> 03:17:03.390
is noninteracting electrons plus
a little bit of coulomb balance

03:17:03.390 --> 03:17:06.080
potential in the background,
jellium basically,

03:17:06.080 --> 03:17:09.480
plus pairwise coulomb forces.

03:17:09.480 --> 03:17:11.395
And it wouldn't work,
and it wouldn't work,

03:17:11.395 --> 03:17:12.270
and it wouldn't work.

03:17:12.270 --> 03:17:15.033
And, finally, I said, well,
it's not going to work.

03:17:15.033 --> 03:17:15.783
This doesn't work.

03:17:15.783 --> 03:17:17.820
It's a great idea,
but it failed.

03:17:17.820 --> 03:17:21.360
So I went in the physics
library at Livermore

03:17:21.360 --> 03:17:24.000
and began reading
books on helium.

03:17:24.000 --> 03:17:25.740
I thought, oh, well,
helium is like this,

03:17:25.740 --> 03:17:27.510
and I could learn from helium.

03:17:27.510 --> 03:17:29.280
And the very first
book I pulled down

03:17:29.280 --> 03:17:33.090
was Gene Feenberg's book
on many body theory.

03:17:33.090 --> 03:17:36.090
And I opened it at
random, and there

03:17:36.090 --> 03:17:40.120
on the very page I had opened
was this wave function.

03:17:40.120 --> 03:17:47.910
It turns out that this
functional form for many body

03:17:47.910 --> 03:17:49.470
problems is used very commonly.

03:17:49.470 --> 03:17:54.600
It's called Jastrow form,
and it's variational.

03:17:54.600 --> 03:17:56.130
So I thought, oh,
my god, that's it.

03:17:56.130 --> 03:17:57.630
The function is an exact.

03:17:57.630 --> 03:18:01.380
Wave functions in many
body physics never are.

03:18:01.380 --> 03:18:04.140
So the thing is variational.

03:18:04.140 --> 03:18:08.190
So I quickly went to
find out how good it was.

03:18:08.190 --> 03:18:11.280
Now, just so you folks
know, what's written here,

03:18:11.280 --> 03:18:13.620
z 1 through z n
are the locations

03:18:13.620 --> 03:18:18.820
of the electrons in the plane
expressed as complex numbers.

03:18:18.820 --> 03:18:22.410
So this is a pairwise
difference raised to a power.

03:18:22.410 --> 03:18:24.977
The power has to
be an odd integer.

03:18:24.977 --> 03:18:27.060
And then because of the
background magnetic field,

03:18:27.060 --> 03:18:31.500
it has to be canceled
by an exponential one

03:18:31.500 --> 03:18:35.040
for each electron, and the
length scale in this experiment

03:18:35.040 --> 03:18:39.130
is the magnetic length
which has been set to 1.

03:18:39.130 --> 03:18:46.140
So, as luck would have it,
I was in a laboratory that

03:18:46.140 --> 03:18:48.480
specializes in plasma physics.

03:18:48.480 --> 03:18:52.050
And the nature of the
calculations that I had to do

03:18:52.050 --> 03:18:56.340
were all the same as those
done in dense plasmas.

03:18:56.340 --> 03:19:04.110
So I went to my plasma buddies
Forrest Rogers and Hugh DeWitt

03:19:04.110 --> 03:19:05.970
and asked them how to calculate.

03:19:05.970 --> 03:19:08.670
And they showed me,
and then one by one,

03:19:08.670 --> 03:19:11.220
things began to fall into place.

03:19:11.220 --> 03:19:15.090
So we squared the wave
function to get the probability

03:19:15.090 --> 03:19:18.150
to find the electrons
at various positions.

03:19:18.150 --> 03:19:19.920
Integrate out all
but one of those

03:19:19.920 --> 03:19:22.530
coordinates, and we get the
density, the charge density

03:19:22.530 --> 03:19:24.870
of the state.

03:19:24.870 --> 03:19:30.630
And, sure enough, it was exactly
uniform out to the boundary,

03:19:30.630 --> 03:19:32.640
and the density is
exactly what we want.

03:19:32.640 --> 03:19:37.740
It's one of the ideal density
of a filled Landau level.

03:19:37.740 --> 03:19:40.110
The first nontrivial
value of n, by the way,

03:19:40.110 --> 03:19:43.440
is 3, which is the 1/3 effect.

03:19:43.440 --> 03:19:47.640
Also, one can integrate out
all but two of the coordinates

03:19:47.640 --> 03:19:50.830
and get what's called
the correlation function.

03:19:50.830 --> 03:19:53.400
And that's important for--

03:19:57.870 --> 03:20:00.340
well, here's what it looks like.

03:20:00.340 --> 03:20:06.690
So what this is is this is the
density of the fluid given that

03:20:06.690 --> 03:20:09.660
as a function of distance,
given that one of the particles

03:20:09.660 --> 03:20:11.910
is at the origin.

03:20:11.910 --> 03:20:14.400
So in the electron
gas lingo, this

03:20:14.400 --> 03:20:19.270
is the exchange correlation
hole of the gas.

03:20:19.270 --> 03:20:22.850
And what you see is that the
electrons avoid each other.

03:20:22.850 --> 03:20:26.500
So if one electron is at the
origin than the other electrons

03:20:26.500 --> 03:20:27.700
avoid it.

03:20:27.700 --> 03:20:29.470
Although, in the m
equals 3 state, which

03:20:29.470 --> 03:20:32.720
is the interesting one,
they pile up a little bit

03:20:32.720 --> 03:20:35.080
at the near neighbor position.

03:20:35.080 --> 03:20:38.350
So once you have this
function, then you

03:20:38.350 --> 03:20:43.405
can weight it by 1 over
R to get the energy.

03:20:46.450 --> 03:20:51.220
Now, just to show you there
was, at the time, a strawman--

03:20:51.220 --> 03:20:53.890
which was Hide Fukuyama's--

03:20:53.890 --> 03:20:56.420
Hide and Phil
Platzman, I guess--

03:20:56.420 --> 03:21:00.640
their Hartree-Fock calculations
for the Wigner crystal.

03:21:00.640 --> 03:21:04.570
And so it was possible to
weight this pair distribution

03:21:04.570 --> 03:21:09.700
function by 1 over R and find
that the wave function I made

03:21:09.700 --> 03:21:11.140
was a little better
energetically

03:21:11.140 --> 03:21:13.374
because it keeps the
particles a little bit

03:21:13.374 --> 03:21:14.665
farther apart than the crystal.

03:21:18.850 --> 03:21:28.110
And so here is total energy as
a function of filling factor.

03:21:30.780 --> 03:21:34.290
Here is the strawman
Wigner crystal energy.

03:21:34.290 --> 03:21:39.150
Down at the bottom is the
1/3 state I constructed.

03:21:39.150 --> 03:21:43.560
1/5 looks like it's
better, and then 1/7

03:21:43.560 --> 03:21:45.900
is a little hard to tell.

03:21:45.900 --> 03:21:47.830
So on the basis of
this calculation,

03:21:47.830 --> 03:21:52.730
I predicted that there should
be one more of these fractions,

03:21:52.730 --> 03:21:54.970
namely 1 at 1/5.

03:21:54.970 --> 03:21:57.825
When I finished this
calculation, I phoned up Horst.

03:21:57.825 --> 03:22:01.410
I said, Horst, Horst, I think
there's another fraction.

03:22:01.410 --> 03:22:03.210
He said, really, what?

03:22:03.210 --> 03:22:05.230
I said, 1/5.

03:22:05.230 --> 03:22:08.170
He said, well, it's close.

03:22:08.170 --> 03:22:09.700
What had happened
in the meantime

03:22:09.700 --> 03:22:11.530
was that these
guys had discovered

03:22:11.530 --> 03:22:15.160
the famous 2/5 state, which,
unfortunately, I did not

03:22:15.160 --> 03:22:16.180
predict.

03:22:16.180 --> 03:22:19.000
And then they began to
find all sorts of fractions

03:22:19.000 --> 03:22:23.020
that I didn't predict
and didn't find 1/5.

03:22:23.020 --> 03:22:29.621
And that was, as my father
used to say, cheap thrills.

03:22:29.621 --> 03:22:31.870
And then they didn't find
it, and they didn't find it,

03:22:31.870 --> 03:22:32.870
and they didn't find it.

03:22:32.870 --> 03:22:38.080
And then, finally, I believe
it was Emilio Mendez found it

03:22:38.080 --> 03:22:40.000
in this experiment.

03:22:40.000 --> 03:22:41.740
Now, there are better--

03:22:41.740 --> 03:22:42.570
wait, wait.

03:22:42.570 --> 03:22:44.390
[LAUGHTER]

03:22:44.390 --> 03:22:47.050
Wait-- there are
better experiments.

03:22:47.050 --> 03:22:50.710
I just wanted to show
this one to demonstrate

03:22:50.710 --> 03:22:53.740
the lengths to which theorists
will go to declare victory

03:22:53.740 --> 03:22:56.740
of their theories.

03:22:56.740 --> 03:23:00.160
In fact, modern samples
have a nice plateau here,

03:23:00.160 --> 03:23:04.270
although it is one of the
weakest ones ever found.

03:23:04.270 --> 03:23:07.900
Well, let's just
get that right off.

03:23:07.900 --> 03:23:11.950
Now, what about the
fractionally charts excitations?

03:23:11.950 --> 03:23:14.090
Turns out, you get
those for free.

03:23:14.090 --> 03:23:20.510
Once you have a uniform
state with an energy gap,

03:23:20.510 --> 03:23:22.510
then you can imagine a
little thought experiment

03:23:22.510 --> 03:23:26.890
where you poke the sample with
an infinitely thin solenoid,

03:23:26.890 --> 03:23:31.170
adiabatically wind
a little flux--

03:23:31.170 --> 03:23:34.090
a magnetic flux through
it, a whole flux quantum.

03:23:34.090 --> 03:23:38.260
And then once you've done
that, again, the Hamiltonian

03:23:38.260 --> 03:23:42.010
has returned to itself just
like it is in the loop problem.

03:23:42.010 --> 03:23:43.630
And so you can
remove the solenoid

03:23:43.630 --> 03:23:45.580
by gauge transformation.

03:23:45.580 --> 03:23:51.580
And this process gives the
next iteration of charge

03:23:51.580 --> 03:23:55.540
plus or minus 1/3, depending
on which way you wind.

03:23:55.540 --> 03:23:57.430
The basic reason for
this is the following.

03:23:57.430 --> 03:23:59.770
That the winding
process does something

03:23:59.770 --> 03:24:02.770
complicated near the solenoid
you don't understand.

03:24:02.770 --> 03:24:06.880
But far away from the solenoid,
the effect is very simple.

03:24:06.880 --> 03:24:09.620
It's exactly the same as in the
integral quantum Hall effect.

03:24:09.620 --> 03:24:14.450
It just takes the state and
moves it over by one orbital.

03:24:14.450 --> 03:24:18.910
And so the net
charge transported

03:24:18.910 --> 03:24:21.460
through an imaginary
Gauss's law box here

03:24:21.460 --> 03:24:25.940
is the average charge per
orbital of the ground state,

03:24:25.940 --> 03:24:29.130
which, in this case, was 1/3.

03:24:29.130 --> 03:24:31.770
One thing led to
another, and I cooked up

03:24:31.770 --> 03:24:35.970
these variational wave functions
for the positive and negative

03:24:35.970 --> 03:24:38.480
quasi particle.

03:24:38.480 --> 03:24:41.230
Z0 here is not a variable.

03:24:41.230 --> 03:24:45.780
It's a place locating the
center of this particle.

03:24:45.780 --> 03:24:46.830
So it's a quantum number.

03:24:50.000 --> 03:24:52.220
These wave functions
came out of the blue.

03:24:52.220 --> 03:24:54.110
They were just the
simplest approximations

03:24:54.110 --> 03:24:55.859
I could think of that
would look something

03:24:55.859 --> 03:24:57.230
like this thought experiment.

03:24:57.230 --> 03:25:00.170
Later, Duncan
Haldane and Ed Rezayi

03:25:00.170 --> 03:25:03.050
did numerical calculations
on the problem

03:25:03.050 --> 03:25:06.320
and found out these wave
functions were vastly better

03:25:06.320 --> 03:25:07.920
than they had any right to be.

03:25:07.920 --> 03:25:10.610
So these are actually
pretty good representations

03:25:10.610 --> 03:25:16.610
of the problem with
coulomb interactions.

03:25:16.610 --> 03:25:20.135
What these particles
look like is this.

03:25:20.135 --> 03:25:21.450
This is what they look like.

03:25:21.450 --> 03:25:25.640
This is a plot of charge
density versus how far you

03:25:25.640 --> 03:25:27.710
are from the center
of the particle.

03:25:27.710 --> 03:25:30.830
And we want to look at
the solid line here.

03:25:30.830 --> 03:25:33.110
That's the positively
charged one.

03:25:33.110 --> 03:25:34.761
What you see is near
the center of it,

03:25:34.761 --> 03:25:37.010
there is a place where the
charge density of the fluid

03:25:37.010 --> 03:25:38.640
is missing.

03:25:38.640 --> 03:25:42.140
And when you add up the
deficit, it's exactly 1/3.

03:25:42.140 --> 03:25:45.460
The quasi hole wave function
is this dashed line,

03:25:45.460 --> 03:25:46.820
and it's the opposite.

03:25:46.820 --> 03:25:50.420
The charge density of the vacuum
near the center is in excess.

03:25:50.420 --> 03:25:52.850
And when you add it up,
the amount in excess

03:25:52.850 --> 03:25:55.040
is exactly 1/3.

03:25:55.040 --> 03:25:58.280
Now, with these wave
functions, then it's

03:25:58.280 --> 03:26:03.440
possible to compute the coulomb
repulsion of the piled up

03:26:03.440 --> 03:26:06.470
charge with itself.

03:26:06.470 --> 03:26:10.460
And then compare it with
measurements of the energy

03:26:10.460 --> 03:26:13.860
to make such a particle.

03:26:13.860 --> 03:26:18.590
These measurements--
measurements which do that,

03:26:18.590 --> 03:26:22.020
or which we believe do
that-- are shown here.

03:26:22.020 --> 03:26:24.110
This is a plot of the
parallel resistance

03:26:24.110 --> 03:26:29.010
versus 1 over temperature
down in the dead center

03:26:29.010 --> 03:26:32.180
in a plateau.

03:26:32.180 --> 03:26:34.580
And what you see is,
as you cool it off,

03:26:34.580 --> 03:26:36.710
which goes to the
right, there's a region

03:26:36.710 --> 03:26:40.820
where you get Arrhenius
behavior, transitioning

03:26:40.820 --> 03:26:43.910
to what we call variable
range hopping behavior

03:26:43.910 --> 03:26:46.580
at lower temperatures.

03:26:46.580 --> 03:26:51.000
Both of these behaviors have
lore associated with them.

03:26:51.000 --> 03:26:53.210
This is a strong
localization effect,

03:26:53.210 --> 03:26:56.840
and this is what you expect
to get very generally

03:26:56.840 --> 03:27:01.460
with thermal activation of
particles from a chemical

03:27:01.460 --> 03:27:05.230
potential up to a mobility edge.

03:27:05.230 --> 03:27:07.670
The mobility edge distance
ought to be something

03:27:07.670 --> 03:27:10.650
like the gap of the state.

03:27:10.650 --> 03:27:14.390
So one can take this slope and
convert it into an energy gap

03:27:14.390 --> 03:27:19.460
and compare it with
what one gets in theory.

03:27:19.460 --> 03:27:23.690
Now, when this was first
done, it didn't work so well.

03:27:23.690 --> 03:27:30.100
This is a plot of
measured activation

03:27:30.100 --> 03:27:34.840
gap versus field strength.

03:27:34.840 --> 03:27:36.640
Here, the measurements
down here--

03:27:36.640 --> 03:27:40.500
and the theory is
this dash line.

03:27:40.500 --> 03:27:47.320
However, shortly
thereafter, Alan MacDonald

03:27:47.320 --> 03:27:50.110
realized that the
model is too crude.

03:27:50.110 --> 03:27:51.760
There's a big effect
missing, which

03:27:51.760 --> 03:27:59.502
is the thickness of the electron
gas in the vertical direction.

03:27:59.502 --> 03:28:00.710
So it has a finite thickness.

03:28:00.710 --> 03:28:04.110
And when one takes into
account, a good hefty fraction

03:28:04.110 --> 03:28:06.630
of the deficit goes away.

03:28:06.630 --> 03:28:09.360
And the rest of it--

03:28:09.360 --> 03:28:11.220
at least, I just
described too well

03:28:11.220 --> 03:28:13.440
being good enough
for government work--

03:28:13.440 --> 03:28:18.540
because these this relation
of the mobility edge

03:28:18.540 --> 03:28:21.174
energy to the actual
gap is a little

03:28:21.174 --> 03:28:22.215
vague in the first place.

03:28:24.870 --> 03:28:28.620
Being comparable in size
is enough, especially

03:28:28.620 --> 03:28:30.387
when the trend is right.

03:28:30.387 --> 03:28:32.970
Notice, everybody, please, that
the energy scale we're talking

03:28:32.970 --> 03:28:34.860
about here is quite low--

03:28:34.860 --> 03:28:38.730
quite low compared with the
natural coulomb energy scale.

03:28:38.730 --> 03:28:44.070
So the fact that has this
trend with magnetic field

03:28:44.070 --> 03:28:48.940
and is also the right
size is very significant.

03:28:48.940 --> 03:28:50.460
So we got that right.

03:28:50.460 --> 03:28:58.380
Now, the last thing I want to
talk about is gauge forces.

03:28:58.380 --> 03:29:02.300
It somehow came to
pass in the development

03:29:02.300 --> 03:29:07.100
of composite fermions, which
are perfectly right in the way

03:29:07.100 --> 03:29:10.580
that the following
amazing property

03:29:10.580 --> 03:29:14.940
of these quasi particles
got overlooked.

03:29:14.940 --> 03:29:18.780
I think this has
always struck me

03:29:18.780 --> 03:29:21.210
as one of the most
important and most amazing

03:29:21.210 --> 03:29:23.280
properties of these objects.

03:29:23.280 --> 03:29:24.900
And that is that
they exert forces

03:29:24.900 --> 03:29:27.840
on each other that are
velocity dependent.

03:29:27.840 --> 03:29:33.630
This was first figured out by
Frank Wilczek and Dan Arovas

03:29:33.630 --> 03:29:37.640
and Bob Schrieffer who took
the trouble of adiabatically

03:29:37.640 --> 03:29:41.630
exchanging two of these
quasi particles theoretically

03:29:41.630 --> 03:29:44.270
and discovering that
the so-called berry

03:29:44.270 --> 03:29:48.260
phase for adiabatic
exchange was a fraction.

03:29:48.260 --> 03:29:53.930
In this experiment, you
get an odd multiple of pi

03:29:53.930 --> 03:29:58.130
when the particles are fermions,
an even multiple of pi when

03:29:58.130 --> 03:29:59.510
they're bosons.

03:29:59.510 --> 03:30:03.320
This particular
multiple was either one.

03:30:03.320 --> 03:30:05.075
Between, it's a
fraction, and a fraction

03:30:05.075 --> 03:30:11.300
is associated with the
charge of the particle.

03:30:11.300 --> 03:30:13.340
What that means
physically is that when

03:30:13.340 --> 03:30:16.970
one of these particles moves
in the presence of another,

03:30:16.970 --> 03:30:23.060
it feels a fictitious vector
potential as though there were

03:30:23.060 --> 03:30:26.750
a solenoid being carried by the
stationary particle carrying

03:30:26.750 --> 03:30:30.410
a fraction of the
elementary flux quantum

03:30:30.410 --> 03:30:33.800
where the fraction is
associated with the charge.

03:30:33.800 --> 03:30:36.830
Now, the really neat thing about
fractional statistics was that

03:30:36.830 --> 03:30:43.640
it was figured out about
the same time-- and I think,

03:30:43.640 --> 03:30:45.170
actually, before--

03:30:45.170 --> 03:30:50.330
empirically by Bert Halperin
through graphs like this.

03:30:50.330 --> 03:30:54.560
Bert figured out that if the
fractional statistics were

03:30:54.560 --> 03:30:59.540
present, then the quasi
particles themselves could

03:30:59.540 --> 03:31:04.160
recondense into new fractions.

03:31:04.160 --> 03:31:05.660
And those fractions
would come out

03:31:05.660 --> 03:31:10.910
to be the observed ones, namely
2/5, 3/7, and so forth, If?

03:31:10.910 --> 03:31:15.840
They had these solenoidal
forces on them.

03:31:15.840 --> 03:31:19.271
So this is a total energy
calculation pulled out

03:31:19.271 --> 03:31:20.270
of one of Bert's papers.

03:31:20.270 --> 03:31:22.394
And we don't have to worry
about the details of it.

03:31:22.394 --> 03:31:24.590
Just notice that it has
some interesting features

03:31:24.590 --> 03:31:30.380
at the fractions at which the
so-called hierarchical states

03:31:30.380 --> 03:31:32.450
occur.

03:31:32.450 --> 03:31:36.770
Now, my interpretation
of this state of affairs

03:31:36.770 --> 03:31:42.920
has really not changed
over the many years,

03:31:42.920 --> 03:31:49.460
namely that the observation of
these fractions other than 1/3

03:31:49.460 --> 03:31:54.890
amounts to experimental
proof that the gauge

03:31:54.890 --> 03:31:58.530
forces are there.

03:31:58.530 --> 03:32:00.450
I mean, the gauge
forces actually

03:32:00.450 --> 03:32:02.820
are emergent in
this problem, even

03:32:02.820 --> 03:32:05.760
though there is more than
one way to describe it.

03:32:05.760 --> 03:32:08.940
The physics of emergent
velocity dependent forces

03:32:08.940 --> 03:32:11.820
is definitely present
in the problem

03:32:11.820 --> 03:32:13.980
and has physical
measurable effect.

03:32:16.710 --> 03:32:19.630
Now, we go back to the premise.

03:32:19.630 --> 03:32:24.400
Now, after all is said and
done, what have we learned?

03:32:24.400 --> 03:32:27.270
Well, like most wonderful
things in physics,

03:32:27.270 --> 03:32:31.740
this particular discovery
has implications.

03:32:31.740 --> 03:32:33.380
It was not expected.

03:32:33.380 --> 03:32:36.120
It was completely
out of the blue.

03:32:36.120 --> 03:32:41.860
It has very many
interesting aspects,

03:32:41.860 --> 03:32:45.240
particularly those
relevant to small devices

03:32:45.240 --> 03:32:49.110
in solid state physics,
semiconductor engineering,

03:32:49.110 --> 03:32:50.920
and so forth.

03:32:50.920 --> 03:32:55.200
But the thing that matters
to me mostly as a theorist

03:32:55.200 --> 03:33:00.720
is the bigger issue of where
the strange rules of the vacuum

03:33:00.720 --> 03:33:03.360
might come from.

03:33:03.360 --> 03:33:05.070
And always, when you
have an experiment,

03:33:05.070 --> 03:33:07.740
god is on your side.

03:33:07.740 --> 03:33:09.510
In this case, we do
have experiments.

03:33:09.510 --> 03:33:11.400
We have accurate
quantization, which

03:33:11.400 --> 03:33:15.870
is telling us what
that there are, indeed,

03:33:15.870 --> 03:33:17.970
fractionally charged
objects in the world that

03:33:17.970 --> 03:33:20.110
are collective in nature.

03:33:20.110 --> 03:33:24.870
They carry a quantum
of charge that

03:33:24.870 --> 03:33:29.030
is as exact as the
electric charge itself,

03:33:29.030 --> 03:33:31.170
of the electron itself.

03:33:31.170 --> 03:33:35.410
And they also have very
powerful forces between them,

03:33:35.410 --> 03:33:38.730
which are not postulated in the
underlying equations of motion

03:33:38.730 --> 03:33:43.780
but simply emerge a new
vacuum and a new kind--

03:33:43.780 --> 03:33:48.120
fundamentally new kind
of quantum emergence.

03:33:48.120 --> 03:33:51.300
At least for me, and I hope
for you too eventually,

03:33:51.300 --> 03:33:55.920
this has been an exceedingly
thought-provoking thing.

03:33:55.920 --> 03:34:02.070
And I believe and hope that it
will have major implications

03:34:02.070 --> 03:34:06.180
for physics of all kinds as
we move into the next century

03:34:06.180 --> 03:34:07.159
and millennium.

03:34:07.159 --> 03:34:07.659
All right.

03:34:07.659 --> 03:34:09.138
That's all I have to say.

03:34:09.138 --> 03:34:10.124
Thank you very much.

03:34:10.124 --> 03:34:22.435
[APPLAUSE]

03:34:22.435 --> 03:34:23.435
KASTNER: Thank you, Bob.

03:34:23.435 --> 03:34:25.010
That was a very beautiful talk.

03:34:25.010 --> 03:34:27.630
And we have time, I think,
for a couple of questions.

03:34:27.630 --> 03:34:28.380
Yes?

03:34:28.380 --> 03:34:29.179
Patrick?

03:34:29.179 --> 03:34:34.043
AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]

03:34:34.043 --> 03:34:34.668
LAUGHLIN: Yeah.

03:34:42.652 --> 03:34:43.650
Maybe I lied.

03:34:47.516 --> 03:34:48.141
Sorry, Patrick.

03:34:48.141 --> 03:34:52.632
We have a parody problem.

03:34:52.632 --> 03:34:55.170
Wait, wait.

03:34:55.170 --> 03:34:58.230
Yeah, here we go.

03:34:58.230 --> 03:34:59.285
Here we go.

03:34:59.285 --> 03:35:02.720
KASTNER: The picture
that had the loop?

03:35:02.720 --> 03:35:05.648
LAUGHLIN: Right.

03:35:05.648 --> 03:35:10.040
AUDIENCE: So I also try
to teach this in my class,

03:35:10.040 --> 03:35:12.968
but I've never been
able to move on

03:35:12.968 --> 03:35:15.896
because I don't understand how
you can go from the derivative

03:35:15.896 --> 03:35:17.360
to the discreet--

03:35:17.360 --> 03:35:18.710
LAUGHLIN: Excellent question.

03:35:18.710 --> 03:35:21.380
Let me answer that now so that
your students will understand

03:35:21.380 --> 03:35:23.270
this henceforth.

03:35:23.270 --> 03:35:24.930
OK, let me answer
this now, Patrick.

03:35:24.930 --> 03:35:27.770
Because you know--
you all should

03:35:27.770 --> 03:35:29.810
know that Patrick and
I have been arguing

03:35:29.810 --> 03:35:31.435
about this for 10 years.

03:35:31.435 --> 03:35:32.710
AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]

03:35:32.710 --> 03:35:34.770
LAUGHLIN: Well, yeah, right.

03:35:34.770 --> 03:35:37.820
My hair is grayer than
yours, so I can't admit it.

03:35:37.820 --> 03:35:42.280
The answer, of course, is
that when the loop is small so

03:35:42.280 --> 03:35:45.430
that there's a
Bohm-Aharonov effect, then

03:35:45.430 --> 03:35:48.676
the Hall conductance
is not quantized.

03:35:48.676 --> 03:35:49.640
AUDIENCE: That true?

03:35:49.640 --> 03:35:50.604
LAUGHLIN: Yep.

03:35:50.604 --> 03:35:53.496
AUDIENCE: Are you
predicting [INAUDIBLE]??

03:35:53.496 --> 03:35:55.495
LAUGHLIN: Yes, but that's
a no-brainer, Patrick.

03:35:55.495 --> 03:35:59.950
AUDIENCE: No, but then
it tries to [INAUDIBLE]..

03:35:59.950 --> 03:36:01.229
LAUGHLIN: Wait, wait, wait.

03:36:01.229 --> 03:36:02.520
Patrick, this is already known.

03:36:02.520 --> 03:36:04.700
If you have something
that's one or two atoms,

03:36:04.700 --> 03:36:07.050
and one or two
magnetic lengths big,

03:36:07.050 --> 03:36:09.205
there isn't any
quantization of anything.

03:36:09.205 --> 03:36:11.580
AUDIENCE: So the question is,
how does it depend on help?

03:36:11.580 --> 03:36:12.820
LAUGHLIN: Ah, interesting.

03:36:12.820 --> 03:36:14.910
Now, interesting question.

03:36:14.910 --> 03:36:20.260
Now, nobody knows.

03:36:20.260 --> 03:36:22.110
Patrick, you know when you--

03:36:22.110 --> 03:36:22.789
I'm sorry.

03:36:22.789 --> 03:36:23.580
I'm preaching here.

03:36:23.580 --> 03:36:26.520
Look, I don't know
how it depends on l.

03:36:26.520 --> 03:36:32.940
What I know is that when
the sample is too small,

03:36:32.940 --> 03:36:34.110
you can see it.

03:36:34.110 --> 03:36:38.070
It's there, and therefore, the
quantization argument is false.

03:36:38.070 --> 03:36:41.790
So one has to be in
the thermodynamic limit

03:36:41.790 --> 03:36:43.890
for the argument to work.

03:36:43.890 --> 03:36:46.635
And that's because localization
is a thermodynamic concept.

03:36:49.230 --> 03:36:53.130
Now, you're absolutely
right that the disappearance

03:36:53.130 --> 03:36:55.830
of the Bohm-Aharonov effect
in the thermodynamic limit

03:36:55.830 --> 03:36:57.300
is part of the argument.

03:37:00.950 --> 03:37:04.430
And I guess the
best answer I can

03:37:04.430 --> 03:37:06.230
give you is, like
localizations-- see,

03:37:06.230 --> 03:37:09.050
I can't prove that either.

03:37:09.050 --> 03:37:14.990
But the scaling hypothesis leads
me to plus experimental facts,

03:37:14.990 --> 03:37:18.770
lead me to believe very
strongly in localization.

03:37:18.770 --> 03:37:20.930
And so by the same
token, I'd say

03:37:20.930 --> 03:37:24.920
that if we have a loop
that's a centimeter in size,

03:37:24.920 --> 03:37:30.990
I assure you that you will never
see the Bohm-Aharonov effect.

03:37:30.990 --> 03:37:31.590
I assure you.

03:37:31.590 --> 03:37:33.257
AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]

03:37:33.257 --> 03:37:33.840
LAUGHLIN: Yes.

03:37:33.840 --> 03:37:36.630
Now, Ray-- now, Ray--

03:37:36.630 --> 03:37:41.070
I made Ray a bet that
an effect that he saw

03:37:41.070 --> 03:37:42.970
was due to-- what did I say?

03:37:42.970 --> 03:37:46.770
I said it was time-dependent
delays and transport.

03:37:46.770 --> 03:37:48.750
And Ray made me
this bet in public

03:37:48.750 --> 03:37:51.080
at a semiconductor meeting.

03:37:51.080 --> 03:37:57.440
And then, well, should I tell
the rest of the story, Ray?

03:37:57.440 --> 03:37:58.640
Well, I don't know.

03:37:58.640 --> 03:38:01.070
I think probably we ought
to pay each other $50

03:38:01.070 --> 03:38:02.910
and then go have a beer.

03:38:02.910 --> 03:38:07.430
What actually happened
was the experiment was--

03:38:07.430 --> 03:38:10.920
the voltage in the experiment
was driven a little too hard.

03:38:10.920 --> 03:38:15.590
And the effect was an
artifact of the measurement.

03:38:15.590 --> 03:38:17.345
So who is culpable there?

03:38:17.345 --> 03:38:21.530
AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]

03:38:21.530 --> 03:38:22.270
LAUGHLIN: True.

03:38:22.270 --> 03:38:23.420
It's a different artifact.

03:38:23.420 --> 03:38:27.480
But I say if you demand the
$100 under those circumstances,

03:38:27.480 --> 03:38:28.892
you are a scoundrel.

03:38:31.490 --> 03:38:34.636
I think we should buy each other
a beer and call it a day, Ray.

03:38:34.636 --> 03:38:37.612
[LAUGHTER]

03:38:37.612 --> 03:38:38.610
AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]

03:38:38.610 --> 03:38:39.590
LAUGHLIN: Right.

03:38:39.590 --> 03:38:41.340
KASTNER: I think on
that note, let's thank

03:38:41.340 --> 03:38:43.140
Bob for a beautiful report.

03:38:43.140 --> 03:38:44.990
[APPLAUSE]

